System audit 2026-07-23 found capture healthy but durability broken; Phase 1 remediation executed same day (pre-approved by Eric).

**Now remote-backed (all private GitHub repos under erash11):**
- SecondBrain (212 outstanding files committed+pushed 7/23)
- claude-global-memory (~\.claude\global-memory)
- claude-skills (~\.claude\skills)
- dotclaude (~\.claude config: settings, hooks, agents, keybindings, skills-archive/audit — whitelist .gitignore; .credentials.json and token-dashboard.db deliberately excluded; new config files must be added to the whitelist or they silently won't back up)
- morning-briefing, ZoteroInjestion (repos existed, remotes created)
- claude-memory-compiler → forked to erash11 (origin=fork, upstream=coleam00); the 4 local patch commits (flush retry, uv.lock, errors.log escalation) pushed. Fork is PUBLIC (inherits upstream) — code only, daily logs untracked, verified safe 7/23.
- ForcePlate + Risk_Stratification fast-forwarded to their PR #1 merges; DataBase_GPS pushed.

**Phase 2 DONE (7/23, pre-approved):** scheduled task `KeystoneOS-DailyBackup` (daily 06:15, verified live via scheduler run) executes `~\.claude\scripts\daily-backup.ps1`: auto-commits+pushes the 4 memory repos (SecondBrain, dotclaude, claude-skills, claude-global-memory; refuses to merge diverged repos — escalates to .errors.log) and robocopy /MIR snapshots: personal context (~\.claude\projects, ~\.codex memories/sessions/agents/sqlite, ~\.gemini) → personal GOOGLE DRIVE `G:\My Drive\Backups\Machine` (verified 433 MB / 2,305 files 7/23); non-repo DEV folders (~1.9 GB) → Baylor OneDrive `Backups\DEV-NonRepo`. Sensitivity split is deliberate: personal context never on employer storage. KEY DISCOVERY 7/23: personal OneDrive account is NOT signed in on this machine — C:\Users\eric_rash\OneDrive is a dead local folder; Google Drive for Desktop (gmail) is the working personal cloud. RESTORE.md is human-facing (new-machine + Windows→Mac scenarios), mirrored daily to G:\My Drive\Backups\RESTORE.md; canonical at github.com/erash11/dotclaude. gws CLI reinstalled 7/23; re-authed 7/24 with FULL drive scope (read/write, Eric's explicit request) + calendar.readonly on eric.rash11@gmail.com — write round-trip verified (create+delete via API); note gws --upload only accepts files under the cwd; cloud-side backup verification is LIVE in stack-doctor (backup-cloud-* codes): queries RESTORE.md's Drive-side modifiedTime via gws as a DriveFS sync heartbeat. gws gotchas (documented in stack-doctor SKILL.md): `-s drive` shorthand grants NO scopes (v0.22.5 bug — use explicit full scope URLs), and after re-auth delete `~\.config\gws\token_cache.json` or the stale token 403s. memsearch ETIMEDOUT recurred 7/24 PM → chronic, redesigned: the 06:15 backup task now runs an UNCAPPED full reindex (all 5 hook paths, task limit raised to 2h) and resets the hook's timeout-streak counter; hook alarm threshold raised 3→6. Root cause: heavy-day backlogs + SecondBrain library first-index is an HOURS-scale ONNX embedding job — converges incrementally across nights; searches work meanwhile, newest content just lags until indexed. Gotcha: killing a backgrounded shell orphans its memsearch/python children (found one with 81 CPU-min still running — always check Get-Process memsearch after killed tasks). Cloud-check timezone bug fixed same day (UTC-normalize; had shown -4h ages). Stack doctor gained backup-* issue codes + KeystoneOS-DailyBackup task check. RESTORE.md runbook lives in dotclaude (first repo cloned on new machine). Decision recorded: KeystoneOS PR #16 (draft). Eric's call 7/23: no mono-repo, no git-for-everything — git for evolving code/text, snapshots for data.

**Phase 3 open:** Baylor workdrive PDF/Office extraction (biggest knowledge-access gap), memory-system map page in KeystoneOS. Full audit report: delivered 7/23 (job b734e95c).

